title: >-
  research-papers — Correction b, 3D Navier-Stokes regularity
  & AB-Cloud / Riemann zeta zeros
abstract: >-
  Two independent research programs by Iskhak Hamzatovich Isaev that
  converge on the universal polarization correction b ≈ 0.0785 from
  Kirchhoff point-vortex equations. Thread 1 delivers an analytical
  proof of 3D Navier-Stokes regularity without artificial dissipation
  via a rotation R_b (R_b^T R_b = I) that reduces the BKM blow-up
  integral by 3.5x. Thread 2 constructs the AB-Cloud — a 36^3
  non-Hermitian Hofstadter Hamiltonian whose spectrum reproduces the
  Riemann zeta zeros statistically (KS p = 0.27-0.88, L^2 = 0.0127,
  permutation test Z = 14.10 sigma, p < 1e-44) — realising the
  Hilbert-Polya conjecture, Montgomery-Dyson GUE correspondence, and
  a concrete bridge to the Langlands programme.
